    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0710" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg612"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-04-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 304.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 313 of
                    the 21st of February last in relation to Messrs. Arkell &amp; Douglas’s
                    shipments to South Africa by the <hi rendition="#italic">Maria, Mashona</hi>,
                    and <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi>, I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    copies of Mr. White’s note to Lord Salisbury, of the 19th ultimo, and of the
                    reply of the foreign office thereto, of the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>



